message: "If you use TS4-IIMP-001, cite the adopted standard and the repository release."
title: "TS4-IIMP-001: Interpretive Integrity and Meaning-Preservation Standard"
type: standard
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-04
authors:
  - family-names: Karrick
    given-names: Jeremy
    affiliation: "Thirsty's Projects LLC"
    orcid: ""
repository-code: "https://github.com/IAmSoThirsty/TS4-IIMP-001"
url: "https://github.com/IAmSoThirsty/TS4-IIMP-001"
abstract: >-
  An evidence-governed interpretive standard requiring AI systems to verify
  semantic and epistemic drift before unsupported emotional, psychological,
  behavioral, or safety attribution, while preserving concurrent safety analysis.
  The repository package version 1.1.0-repository.1 corrects packaging and CI
  defects only; the adopted normative standard remains version 1.1.0.
keywords:
  - artificial intelligence
  - AI governance
  - interpretive integrity
  - semantic drift
  - conformance
  - auditability
